# Leaderboards must never be served stale from the edge.
#
# The arcade hall (games/index.html) fetches every board to build the
# "games played / players on the record" counters. It passes cache:'no-store',
# which only governs the BROWSER cache — the edge can still hand back an old
# copy, which shows up as counters that intermittently freeze or go backwards.
# The games themselves bust it with a ?nocache= query string, so this rule is
# mainly for the hall and for each cabinet's static read-fallback.
#
# Was previously pinned to dropblock alone; widened to cover every cabinet.
/games/:game/leaderboard.json
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate
